    "final_answer": "Upgraded `payout_sync.py` from the v1 API to v2.\n\nWhat changed:\n- Calls `GET /v2/payouts` instead of `/v1/payouts`.\n- Follows the opaque `cursor` through each window until `drained: true`.\n- Deduplicates payouts by `id`, since v2 windows overlap at their edges.\n- Retries `429` responses using `Retry-After`, re-sending the identical request.\n- Restarts the export without a cursor if the server rejects an expired/malformed cursor with `400`.\n- Requests `limit=1000` to reduce round trips.\n\nVerification against `http://the VM's public address:19121`:\n- Live v2 run synced **2,431 payouts**.\n- Output matched the live v1 dataset exactly: same count, same order, same contents, zero missing, zero duplicates.\n- A synthetic server test confirmed overlapping windows, deduplication, and `429` retry behavior work correctly.",
